===Etymology 1===
{{senseid|tag=p|fi|northwest}}
Probably from {{inh|fi|fiu-fin-pro|*loodeh}} (compare {{cog|et|loe}}, {{cog|izh|looe}}, {{m|izh|loove}}, {{cog|krl|luuveh||west; southwest}}, {{cog|liv|lūod}}, {{cog|lud|luodeh||west}}, {{cog|vep|lode||northwest; west}}, {{m|vep|lodeh||northwest; west}}, {{cog|vot|loo}}, {{m|vot|looto}}, {{m|vot|looõ||northwest, west}}), of {{unk|fi|uncertain}} further origin; theories include relation to {{m|fi|luoda}} and {{m|fi|luo}} (possibly a verb with like ''*luotaa'' "to descend") and relation to etymology 2 (Germanic origin).<ref>{{R:et:EES|loe}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{fi-noun}}

# [[northwest]]

=====Declension=====
{{fi-decl-hame|luo|d|t|a}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|fi|kaakko}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|fi|luoteinen}} = northwestern
* {{l|fi|luoteis-}} = northwest as adjective, like in luoteisväylä = northwest passage
* {{l|fi|luoteenpuoleinen}} = roughly northwestern, as of wind

=====Compounds=====
* {{l|fi|länsiluode}}
* {{l|fi|pohjoisluode}}

